{"vul":41,"heb":42,"title":"In finem. Intellectus filiis Core.","incipit":"Quemadmodum desiderat cervus","verses":[{"n":2,"la":["Quemadmodum","desiderat","cervus","ad","fontes","aquarum,","ita","desiderat","anima","mea","ad","te,","Deus."],"gl":["as","desires","hart","to","springs","of waters","so","desires","soul","my","to","you","O God"],"en":"As the hart panteth after the fountains of water; so my soul panteth after thee, O God."},{"n":3,"la":["Sitivit","anima","mea","ad","Deum","fortem,","vivum;","quando","veniam,","et","apparebo","ante","faciem","Dei?"],"gl":["has thirsted","soul","my","for","God","strong","living","when","shall I come","and","shall I appear","before","face","of God"],"en":"My soul hath thirsted after the strong living God; when shall I come and appear before the face of God?"},{"n":4,"la":["Fuerunt","mihi","lacrimæ","meæ","panes","die","ac","nocte,","dum","dicitur","mihi","quotidie:","Ubi","est","Deus","tuus?"],"gl":["have been","to me","tears","my","bread","by day","and","night","while","it is said","to me","daily","where","is","God","your"],"en":"My tears have been my bread day and night, whilst it is said to me daily: Where is thy God?"},{"n":5,"la":["Hæc","recordatus","sum,","et","effudi","in","me","animam","meam,","quoniam","transibo","in","locum","tabernaculi","admirabilis,","usque","ad","domum","Dei,","in","voce","exsultationis","et","confessionis,","sonus","epulantis."],"gl":["these things","remembered","I have","and","I poured out","within","me","soul","my","for","I shall pass","into","place","of the tabernacle","wonderful","even","to","house","of God","in","voice","of exultation","and","of praise","sound","of one feasting"],"en":"These things I remembered, and poured out my soul in me: for I shall go over into the place of the wonderful tabernacle, even to the house of God: With the voice of joy and praise; the noise of one feasting."},{"n":6,"la":["Quare","tristis","es,","anima","mea?","et","quare","conturbas","me?","Spera","in","Deo,","quoniam","adhuc","confitebor","illi,","salutare","vultus","mei,"],"gl":["why","sad","are you","soul","my","and","why","you trouble","me","hope","in","God","for","still","I will praise","him","salvation","of face","my"],"en":"Why art thou sad, O my soul? and why dost thou trouble me? Hope in God, for I will still give praise to him: the salvation of my countenance,"},{"n":7,"la":["et","Deus","meus.","Ad","meipsum","anima","mea","conturbata","est:","propterea","memor","ero","tui","de","terra","Jordanis","et","Hermoniim","a","monte","modico."],"gl":["and","God","my","within","myself","soul","my","troubled","is","therefore","mindful","I will be","of you","from","land","of Jordan","and","Hermon","from","hill","little"],"en":"and my God. My soul is troubled within myself: therefore will I remember thee from the land of Jordan and Hermoniim, from the little hill."},{"n":8,"la":["Abyssus","abyssum","invocat,","in","voce","cataractarum","tuarum;","omnia","excelsa","tua,","et","fluctus","tui","super","me","transierunt."],"gl":["deep","deep","calls","in","voice","of floodgates","your","all","heights","your","and","waves","your","over","me","have passed"],"en":"Deep calleth on deep, at the noise of thy flood-gates. All thy heights and thy billows have passed over me."},{"n":9,"la":["In","die","mandavit","Dominus","misericordiam","suam,","et","nocte","canticum","ejus;","apud","me","oratio","Deo","vitæ","meæ."],"gl":["in","day","commanded","Lord","mercy","his","and","by night","song","his","with","me","prayer","to God","of life","my"],"en":"In the daytime the Lord hath commanded his mercy; and a canticle to him in the night. With me is prayer to the God of my life."},{"n":10,"la":["Dicam","Deo:","Susceptor","meus","es;","quare","oblitus","es","mei?","et","quare","contristatus","incedo,","dum","affligit","me","inimicus?"],"gl":["I will say","to God","upholder","my","you are","why","forgotten","have you","me","and","why","saddened","do I walk","while","afflicts","me","enemy"],"en":"I will say to God: Thou art my support. Why hast thou forgotten me? and why go I mourning, whilst my enemy afflicteth me?"},{"n":11,"la":["Dum","confringuntur","ossa","mea,","exprobraverunt","mihi","qui","tribulant","me","inimici","mei,","dum","dicunt","mihi","per","singulos","dies:","Ubi","est","Deus","tuus?"],"gl":["while","are broken","bones","my","have reproached","me","who","trouble","me","enemies","my","while","they say","to me","through","each","day","where","is","God","your"],"en":"Whilst my bones are broken, my enemies who trouble me have reproached me; Whilst they say to me day by day: Where is thy God?"},{"n":12,"la":["Quare","tristis","es,","anima","mea?","et","quare","conturbas","me?","Spera","in","Deo,","quoniam","adhuc","confitebor","illi,","salutare","vultus","mei,","et","Deus","meus."],"gl":["why","sad","are you","soul","my","and","why","you trouble","me","hope","in","God","for","still","I will praise","him","salvation","of face","my","and","God","my"],"en":"Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why dost thou disquiet me? Hope thou in God, for I will still give praise to him: the salvation of my countenance, and my God."}]}